# gdi32, win32u, winex11.drv: Get functions get_dib_info_size in sync.
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/11879 state=opened
# I received a ASan-unix report of a memcpy copying 48 bytes from a 40 bytes allocation. 

This difference originates from different versions of the function `get_dib_info_size` being used for allocation and for copying.

Should these functions stay in sync?

CC: @alexhenrie, @jacek 

